Coding conventions for this repo are defined in @AGENTS.md.

Apply them to every `.ts` and `.svelte` file:

- Bun-first (no `npm` / `npx` / `node`).
- Svelte 5 runes mode: `$props`, `$state`, `$derived`, `$effect` — never
  `export let`, `$:`, or `on:click`. Use `{@render children()}`, not `<slot />`.
- SvelteKit data fetching in `+page.server.ts` `load` functions. Service-role
  Supabase key is server-only; do not ship it to the browser.
- Elysia route handlers stay thin — parse, delegate to a function in
  `@orbit/shared` or `apps/bot/src/process.ts`, return JSON.
- Telegraf bot has a single-user guard (`TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USER_ID`). Preserve it.
- All env reads through [packages/shared/src/env.ts](packages/shared/src/env.ts).
- All shared types from [packages/shared/src/types.ts](packages/shared/src/types.ts).
- No `any` in TypeScript. No DDD layers. No client-side state libraries.
- Schema changes go through new files in `supabase/migrations/`.

When writing Svelte code, use the Svelte MCP server tools (`list-sections`,
`get-documentation`, `svelte-autofixer`) before returning code to the user.
